HYP-2691 / T927 -- LRC14 exact sector-state transfer DP
Arithmetic: exact Fractions over common sector-wall refinements.
Preserved predicate: final p0(E) <= cap_k.
Destroyed data: actual continuous time after quotienting each wall atom to a missed-sector state.
Assumption challenged: proof vertices need not be runners; here they are DP states and insertion schedules.

EXACT INSERTION RECURRENCE
  Adding one speed can remove at most one missed inner sector on any wall atom.
  Therefore delta p0 is exactly the mass of atoms where the prefix misses one
  sector and the new speed lands in that sector.  The transition matrix is
  lower triangular in missed-sector inclusion, with rank-one atom moves.

